extraction_notes: |
  - WB6 printed 146-147 (cache p147-p148), read from the text layer and checked
    against 150 dpi renders of both pages. The text layer reads the M.D.C.
    formula as "P.E.xS"; the ink is P.E. x5. Jaguar''s M.D.C. is printed without
    a plus sign ("1D4X10 M.D.C.") where every other totem prints one; read as a
    bonus like the rest. Falcon''s bullet is lost in the text layer, present in ink.
  - The class sits in "The Rain Forest" section beside the Tribal Shaman; no
    S.D.C. or hit point formula is printed. Stored men_of_arms true and
    occ_group men-of-arms: a champion-warrior class with no spell or psionic
    ladder, grouped as Spirit West''s Totem Warrior is.
  - Name and id: `totem-warrior` is Spirit West''s, so the id carries
    -south-american after the -russian precedent, and the name carries
    "(South American)" after "Traditional Gypsy Thief (Russian)".
  - xp_table from the "Voodoo Priest, Jungle Elf & Totem Warrior" ladder,
    printed 168 (cache p169); lower bounds stored, no misprint.
  - Totems: the book''s seven Amazon animals (Anaconda, Crocodile, Falcon, Frog,
    Jaguar, Monkey, Tapir) are NOT Spirit West''s forty North American totems
    and are not rows in the shared `totems` catalog; the class does not carry
    the `totem:` key and adds no totem rows. They are a special_abilities
    choose-1 group, one ability per animal.
  - Decision: every number a totem grants (attribute dice, M.D.C., Spd, combat
    and save bonuses, skill percentages) exists only while the totem is
    invoked (five minutes per level, six times a day), so none is stored in a
    `bonuses` block, which would apply it permanently. They are in each
    ability''s description. The same holds for the invoked state''s own
    P.E. x5 + 10/level M.D.C. and supernatural P.S. (the Totem Gifts ability);
    no mdc_base or mdc_from_hp_sdc is stored, since out of the invocation the
    warrior is an ordinary S.D.C. human.
  - Bonuses stored (ability 2, always on): +2 vs possession and mind control,
    +2 vs magic as spell_magic 2 and ritual_magic 2, +2 vs disease, +3 vs
    horror factor.
  - Skills: base = catalog base + printed bonus. Monster/Demon Lore ->
    Lore: Demons & Monsters; Track Humans and Monsters -> Tracking (people);
    Track Animals -> Track & Trap Animals; Dancing -> Dance. Creole is
    Language: Other at 98%. W.P. Archery and Targeting is stored as both
    W.P. Archery and W.P. Targeting, the two rows the catalog splits it into.
  - Hand to Hand: Expert may change to Martial Arts for one "other" skill;
    nothing else is offered.
  - Related: eight, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. The book''s Pilot line
    ("Boating, horsemanship and horsemanship: exotic animals only (+15%)") is
    split: Boating as the three small-boat Pilot rows, horsemanship as the
    Horsemanship category''s General and Exotic Animals rows, both +15%.
    Technical excludes Computer Operation, Computer Programming and
    Photography. Secondary: four, from the same list without bonuses.
  - Equipment: the two weapons of choice are a choose-2 over this book''s
    lesser biomancy weapons, the two TW converted energy weapons and the
    Colombian RC-10/RC-15; the spear or bow is a choose-1 (arrows not stored
    separately); "one or two knives" stored as one knife; small bag as
    small-sack; armor a choose-1 of light wood, light chitin or light M.D.C.
    body armor.
  - Money: 1D6x100 credits in trade items, stored as 1d6x100.
---

## Lore

Totem warriors are gifted tribesmen of the Amazon who have gone past finding a spirit guide: they can call their totem animal into their own bodies and take on its superhuman powers. Many South American cultures hold ceremonies in which a warrior finds his guide, usually an animal.

They often work with, or are guided by, a tribal shaman; a typical tribe has one shaman and 1D6 totem warriors. They are honored with special privileges and status, and serve as their people''s champions, defenders and avengers. A few have lost or abandoned their tribes and wander as lone adventurers.

High P.S., P.P. and P.E. are common among them but not required.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'totem-warrior-south-american');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
